>Just out of curiosity--what names do you nethackers out there tend to go by?   
>Do you just use your default login name, out of preference or out of 
>ignorance that you can use another one?  Do you use a name from fiction, or 
>from gaming, or one that you've made up?  Do you use the same name all the 
>time, or a different name for each class, or a different name each time?

	I ALWAYS play a rogue named Khyron...anyone familiar with this char-
acter will understand that I'm not playing rogues in the "thief" sense of the
word.  If my character can get away with it, he'll do it.  >:-) *evil grin*
If it's a peaceful monster, it's a dead monster.  (Shopkeepers & priests
excepting.)  Evil anarchists can be really fun to play, and rogues aren't bad
fighters, either.  (Usually starts with 18 dexterity & 14+ strength.)
	Concerning pet names, I usually name my dog "Cujo" (rare now) or just
"stupid mutt".  (I like how the game knows to capitalize the name if it's at
the beginning of a sentence!)  Dogs are nice because they can steal from shops
and can discern cursed stuff.  Cats are annoying, so I never name them.  I
usually abandon them on level 1, then come back later and kill them after 
they're no longer tame.  Mean, eh?
